<BaseLayout title="Meet Deffy — The human behind the Creature"><article class="inside story-page">
 <PageHeading eyebrow="Beyond the front desk" title="Hi. I’m Deffy." intro="A lifelong PC gamer, self-taught creator, and person behind all the peculiar stuff."/>
 <div class="prose"><p>I’m Deffy Pyah Urz, from New Hampshire. A lifelong PC gamer, aspiring streamer, self-taught creator, and someone who keeps asking whether the defaults really have to stay that way.</p>
 <p>World of Warcraft and League of Legends have been part of my life for years. So have computers, internet friendships, and the question “what if?” Sometimes that question becomes a game. Sometimes it becomes software, music, or an entire fictional universe.</p>
 <p>I like making things, but I don’t need every experiment to become useful, profitable, or particularly sensible. Sometimes an idea is just too ridiculous to leave alone.</p>
 <p>I care about individuality, autonomy, meaningful relationships, and intellectual honesty. I’m curious about psychology, philosophy, artificial intelligence, and what people could become. I also like taking a ridiculous premise much too far.</p>
 <p>That doesn’t make me consistent. I’ve changed my mind, contradicted myself, and failed to live up to things I value. There’s room for that here, too.</p>
 <h2>The person and the worlds.</h2><p>“The Creature of the Internet” is a persona. Defdef is a character. <a href="/astrizda/">Astrizda</a> is a fictional universe I created. I’m the person behind them, with a life that extends beyond what I make.</p>
 <h2>A few doors worth opening.</h2>
 <p><a href="/forge/?category=Game">Games I’m making</a>, <a href="/music/">a listening space taking shape</a>, and <a href="/forge/">the experiments in the Forge</a>. Follow whichever feels interesting.</p>
